      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To calculate straight-line depreciation, first find the depreciable cost by subtracting the salvage value from the original cost: $\\$150,000 - \\$25,000 = \\$125,000$. Next, divide the depreciable cost by the useful life to find the annual depreciation expense: $\\$125,000 / 10 \\text{ years} = \\$12,500$. Therefore, the equipment will depreciate by $\\$12,500$ each year.",
      "source": "target",
